codex
The generated Python is exactly the canonical implementation, and the trusted translator reproduces `solution.mpy` byte-for-byte. My independent test covered 276 positive finite IEEE-754 values (documented example, integer discontinuities, subnormal/min/max cases, and 256 seeded generated values), plus zero/negative/non-finite diagnostics and a missing-argument call; it found zero implementation mismatches and zero mismatches against an independent `math.modf` decimal-part oracle. I’m moving to clean K builds now.
